      "answer": "The regular assessment period (Festsetzungsfrist) for income tax is **four years** [7], and it generally begins at the end of the calendar year in which the tax arose [3].\n\n* **Gesetzlich gilt:** \n  * The standard assessment period is 4 years (§ 169 Abs. 2 Satz 2 Nr. 2 AO) [7].\n  * It starts at the end of the calendar year in which the tax was incurred, or a conditionally incurred tax became unconditional (§ 170 Abs. 1 AO) [3].\n  * If a tax return (Steuererklärung) has to be filed, the period begins at the end of the calendar year in which the tax return is filed, but **at the latest** at the end of the third calendar year following the year the tax arose (§ 170 Abs. 2 Satz 1 Nr. 1 AO) [3].\n  * Extended periods apply in cases of tax evasion (10 years) or reckless tax shortening (5 years) (§ 169 Abs. 2 Satz 2 AO) [7], as well as under various suspension rules (Ablaufhemmung, e.g., § 171 AO)."
    },
